[gd_scene format=3 uid="uid://dy4l52xv6k3wy"]

; The rig's own exerciser — ADR-0217 dec. 4/10, moved here by #744. It ships INSIDE the
; addon: it is the scene that drives the whole sprite rig by hand, and an addon whose
; exerciser lives in the host cannot be exercised where the host is absent (goal #5).
;
; 🔴 THE THREE TEXTURE LINES ARE GONE, NOT MOVED (P4). This scene authored
; `type1_tex`/`wep1_tex`/`eff1_tex` against `res://assets/sprites/textures/{01,WEP1,EFF1}.tga`.
; Carrying them in would have put three host content addresses INSIDE the addon on the
; day #744 drove P4 to zero. They were already dead weight: `SequenceViewer.gd` resolves
; the body sheet through `SpriteRigContentRoot.textures_dir()` and calls
; `sprite_layers.load_sprite_texture()` (:569-571), and `SpriteLayerManager` lazily loads
; WEP1/EFF1 through the same content root — so every texture this viewer has ever shown
; came from the port, and the authored ones only decided what the EDITOR preview looked
; like. Same call as `UnitRig.tscn`'s.

[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://g8nwj3on84po" path="res://addons/exmateria_sprite_rig/viewer/SequenceViewer.gd" id="1_script"]
[ext_resource type="Shader" uid="uid://cw3b5wdcumh7v" path="res://addons/exmateria_sprite_rig/render/unit.gdshader" id="2_shader"]

